{
  "name": "ok_terminal_run",
  "description": "terminal/run and terminal/end: a person ran a shell command from the IDE terminal. They are not tool/call and tool/result - a human command has no model in the loop, the same reason file/write is its own type. The run row is written before the command starts, so a process that dies mid-command has already said what it was running; the end row closes it with the exit code (-1 when no status was reaped, with message saying why), the duration, whether a person cancelled it, and the last 4 KiB of each stream. A command refused before it runs writes neither row: a record that says what ran must not describe something that did not.",
